## 6. UI Logic & Data Flow

### Client draft session (`usePartySession`)

```
localStorage key: cleft-session
{ partyName, partyDate, items[], members[] }
```

- Loaded on mount; auto-saved on every `setSession`
- Default party name: `"Friday Chill Party"`
- Survives refresh; cleared on confirm (except `partyName`)

### Auth flow

```
Login (profile menu) → GET /auth/google → JWT cookie
GET /auth/session → { authenticated: true }
Protected routes (Items/Members/Summary) → AuthGuard → redirect / if no session
Profile + history → require auth
```

### Party confirm flow

```
Items + Members (localStorage) → Summary preview (client math)
Confirm & share → POST /party/confirm → DB + optional slip upload
→ reset items/members, keep partyName → redirect Home
```

### Split algorithm (`bill-display.ts` ↔ `party.service.ts`)

**Per-item fair split** (client preview = server authoritative on confirm):

| Rule | Detail |
|------|--------|
| ALL member | Assigned to every item |
| PARTIAL member | Assigned only to checked items |
| Empty partial | Owes **0 THB** |
| Per item | `price × qty` ÷ number of assignees for that item |
| No assignees | Item skipped (no fallback split) |

### Realtime recalculation

| Screen | Triggers recalc |
|--------|-----------------|
| Members | Name, All/Partial, checkbox toggle |
| Home dashboard | Any session change (shared hook) |
| Summary | Any session change |

All use `computePayerAmounts(items, members)`.

### Toast feedback

Success / error / info toasts for profile save, item CRUD, confirm, logout.

